  "body": "## Problem\n\nA stock-source Face with the catalog mill `EM-0400-2FL` (diameter 4 mm) gets a `Gouge` warning on its last pass when that pass is tangent to the stock edge. The post then refuses the program. The document has no part. The pass is above the stock top. Thus no material is in the way, and the warning looks like a false positive.\n\n## How to see it\n\nFound while working on #1657 (a scratch probe in `crates/app/tests/`, not committed):\n\n1. Make a new world with no part.\n2. Add the tool `EM-0400-2FL`.\n3. Set a stock `StockShape::Box { dx: 64, dy: 64, dz: 32 }` at `pos (30, 30, 0)`. The stock is x and y -2..62, z 0..32.\n4. Create a Face on `SrcRef::Stock`: `stepover 3`, `cut_z 34`, `clearance_z 45`.\n5. Generate it.\n\nThe result:\n\n- The passes run at y = 0, 3, ..., 60, x -4..64.\n- Move 42 (the last pass, `(-4, 60, 34) -> (64, 60, 34)`) gets `Gouge`.\n- The tool edge at y = 60 touches y = 62, the stock edge, exactly.\n\nOther readings:\n\n- `dy 65`, `66` or `70`: no warning.\n- `EM-0600-4FL` and `EM-1000-4FL` with `dy 64`: no warning.\n- `cut_z 30.5`, `31.5`, `34` and stepovers 3, 2.9, 1.5: the same `Gouge`.\n- The first pass at y = 0 is also 2 mm from the stock edge (y = -2), but it gets no warning.\n\nA likely place is the section law `tangency` in `crates/sim/src/verify/section.rs` (`d(center, boundary) >= r - leave - tol` against the region loops). This is not confirmed.\n\nI did not check if this occurs before the merges of PR 1622, PR 1634, PR 1640 and PR 1644. The probe has no part, so the keep law of #1607 is not the cause.\n\n## Done means\n\nThe Face above posts without a warning, or the warning is shown to be correct with a reason. A test in the crate that owns the judgement pins the result. A true gouge near the stock edge is still refused.\n",
